{"id":"SMA-637","uuid":"baa10e3a-b404-425e-828f-ea9f360739d3","title":"ci: a negative control for repo:next-env-drift","description":"`ci/next-env/run.sh` has no `--self-test` and no `--negative-control` arm. It is 82 lines with no flag parsing at all, and `repo:next-env-drift` is a bare `script: 'ci/next-env/run.sh'` (root `moon.yml:135`).

<issue id="d93e1e93-11b7-4f47-84b7-4397ff3bf878" href="https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-512/ts-gateway-console-app-the-ai-gateway-zone">SMA-512</issue> pull request 1 parameterizes the gate over every `ts/apps/*` app and adds a set-equality liveness assertion, but deliberately does **not** add the control arms, because the gate is the last self-scheduled-shaped gate without them and adding them is not free.

## The three registry obligations

Adding `--self-test` or `--negative-control` to the script makes `check_self_scheduled_coverage` in `ci/affected-graph/ci_targets.py` fail `repo:affected-smoke` unless all of these land in the same commit:

1. a `SELF_SCHEDULED_GATES["next-env-drift"]` entry pinning the task's `moon.yml` invocation lines, `set -euo pipefail` included;
2. a `SELF_TASK_EXPECTED_GLOBS` entry listing the task's literal `inputs`, **or** a reasoned `SELF_TASK_GLOBS_EXEMPT` one — holding both is itself reported;
3. the `moon.yml` task rewritten from a bare `script:` to the three-invocation form the other self-scheduled gates use.

## Why it is worth doing

Until then the gate's correctness rests on its loop and its set-equality assertion, with nothing proving the drift assertion can still fire. That is the "a gate that can lie" shape <issue id="0df8d298-14c7-4063-a184-f7c03b63519c" href="https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-601/ci-no-required-check-catches-a-truncated-rscargolock">SMA-601</issue> measured for `ci/cargo-lock-integrity/run.sh`, where deleting one flag turned the gate into the first repairer while it still printed a pass.","priority":{"value":0,"name":"No priority"},"url":"https://linear.app/smaschek/issue/SMA-637/ci-a-negative-control-for-reponext-env-drift","gitBranchName":"feature/sma-637-ci-a-negative-control-for-reponext-env-drift","createdAt":"2026-09-13T10:16:56.114Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-13T10:16:56.114Z","archivedAt":null,"completedAt":null,"startedAt":null,"canceledAt":null,"dueDate":null,"slaStartedAt":null,"slaMediumRiskAt":null,"slaHighRiskAt":null,"slaBreachesAt":null,"status":"Backlog","statusType":"backlog","labels":["area:ops"],"attachments":[],"documents":[],"createdBy":"Sven Maschek","createdById":"ba6021cb-56c5-43aa-9797-fab3599d7ead","project":"Paigasus Polyglot","projectId":"94351cc4-6a23-4c34-a043-2e7f1bfd9ae4","team":"Sven Maschek","teamId":"7178572e-d61f-4cf0-bbcb-4e03c8d9f39e"}

